  "body": "in matrix log\r\n`2018-12-03 22:04:40,859 - synapse.http.matrixfederationclient - 320 - INFO - federation_transaction_transmission_loop-489- {PUT-O-337} [sheen.host] Sending request: PUT matrix://sheen.host/_matrix/federation/v1/send/SOMENUMBER/`\r\n\r\n\r\ndns queries log (dnsmasq)\r\n`Dec  3 22:04:57 mgp dnsmasq[52608]: query[SRV] _matrix._tcp.sheen.host from 127.0.0.1\r\nDec  3 22:04:57 mgp dnsmasq[52608]: forwarded _matrix._tcp.sheen.host to 194.150.168.168`\r\n\r\nTo me there is nothing wrong with these actions,\r\nhowever i find the sheer number of queries to lock down my dnsmasq service with this error:\r\n`dnsmasq: Maximum number of concurrent DNS queries reached (max: 150)`\r\n\r\nI have set this limit to 300 and it seems to work for now.\r\nMaybe it is desirable to slow down the frequency of queries for a less aggressive style.\r\n(Such that it not becomes necessary to increase default limits.)",
